Spec: SecurityThreats

Purpose:
  Threat model for the project. This file defines the threat landscape,
  trust boundaries, and threat categories relevant to the project.

Owns: security\threats.sdd
ThreatCategories:
  STRIDE:
    Spoofing
    Tampering
    Repudiation
    Information Disclosure
    Denial of Service
    Elevation of Privilege

  OWASP Top 10:
    A01:2021 Broken Access Control
    A02:2021 Cryptographic Failures
    A03:2021 Injection
    A04:2021 Insecure Design
    A05:2021 Security Misconfiguration
    A06:2021 Vulnerable and Outdated Components
    A07:2021 Identification and Authentication Failures
    A08:2021 Software and Data Integrity Failures
    A09:2021 Security Logging and Monitoring Failures
    A10:2021 Server-Side Request Forgery

  TrustBoundaries:
    Internet
      ?
    WAF / CDN
      ?
    Load Balancer
      ?
    API Gateway
      ?
    Services
      ?
    Database
      ?
    Secrets Store
    MemoryStore
      ?
      (claude-mem daemon, ChromaDB, SQLite — network-exposed if bound to 0.0.0.0)

  Each boundary is a potential attack surface.

  KnownCVEs:
    - CVE-2026-45829: ChromaDB remote code execution via unauthenticated
      HTTP API (CVSS 9.8, CRITICAL)
      source: hiddenlayer.com/advisory, NVD
      mitigation: Pin ChromaDB >=1.5.8; use Rust server; bind 127.0.0.1
      status: addressed via .sdd/security/levels.sdd L4 controls

    - CVE-2026-45832: ChromaDB tenant isolation bypass
      source: hiddenlayer.com/advisory, NVD
      mitigation: Pin ChromaDB >=1.5.8; tenant isolation enforcement
      status: addressed via .sdd/security/levels.sdd L4 controls

    - CVE-2026-45833: ChromaDB data exfiltration via REST API
      source: hiddenlayer.com/advisory, NVD
      mitigation: Pin ChromaDB >=1.5.8; network policy restrictions
      status: addressed via .sdd/security/levels.sdd L4 controls

    - CVE-2025-32434: PyTorch arbitrary code execution
      source: NVD, HackerOne
      mitigation: Pin PyTorch >=2.2.2; dependency scanning
      status: monitored via .sdd/security/controls.sdd SEC.DEP

    - CVE-2026-1839: Transformers unsafe deserialization
      source: NVD, HuggingFace advisory
      mitigation: Pin transformers >=4.51.0; dependency scanning
      status: monitored via .sdd/security/controls.sdd SEC.DEP

    - CVE-2026-55607: Claude Code RCE
      source: GitHub Security Advisory
      mitigation: Upgrade claude-code >=2.1.65
      status: monitored via .sdd/security/controls.sdd SEC.DEP

  PromptInjectionKnownIssues:
    - "Comment and Control" (CVSS 9.4): Claude Code Security Review,
      Gemini CLI Action, GitHub Copilot Agent vulnerable to PR-title/body
      prompt injection exfiltrating ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / GITHUB_TOKEN
      source: aonanguan/Johns-Hopkins disclosure, April 2026
      mitigation: Admit vulnerability in docs; implement fork-PR gating;
        do NOT interpolate untrusted PR content into LLM prompts
      status: documented in .sdd/gates/security.sdd SemanticReview.CacheFalseGreenMitigation

    - Security-review not hardened against prompt injection (explicit admission)
      source: claude-code-security-review README.md:45
      mitigation: Adopt honest trust caveat; fork-PR gating required
      status: documented in .sdd/gates/security.sdd SemanticReview

    - SDDRA-specific injection vectors (documented in .sdd/security/prompt-injection.sdd):
      PI-001 through PI-010 covering instruction override, role reassignment,
      permission escalation, output forcing, chain injection, encoding bypass,
      semantic context hijacking, tool permission grant, whitespace/Unicode obfuscation
      mitigation: PromptGuard runtime layer (sdd-adapter/security/prompt-guard.ts)
      status: implemented via /sdd-scan --inject and CommandRunner guard

  SupplyChainRisks:
    - Unpinned npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code in CI
      source: claude-code-security-review action.yml:171
      mitigation: Pin to specific version; verify npm integrity
      status: monitored via .sdd/security/controls.sdd SEC.SUPPLY

    - Unpinned system packages (sudo apt-get update)
      source: claude-code-security-review action.yml:173
      mitigation: Use pinned Docker image with pre-installed deps
      status: monitored via .sdd/security/controls.sdd SEC.SUPPLY

    - GitHub Actions restore-keys prefix-match cache poisoning
      source: claude-code-security-review issue #120
      mitigation: run_every_commit=true; sha comparison
      status: addressed in .sdd/gates/security.sdd SemanticReview

  PromptInjectionDefense:
    runtime_layer: PromptGuard (sdd-adapter/security/prompt-guard.ts)
    integration_points:
      - CommandRunner.run(): guard customerPrompt before dispatch
      - HookBridge.processHook(): guard UserPromptSubmit events
    pattern_catalog: PI-001 through PI-010 (.sdd/security/prompt-injection.sdd)
    response_modes:
      BLOCK: halt execution, exit 2, audit payload SHA-256
      WARN: proceed with warning, emit OBS15
      LOG: log finding, proceed normally
    evasion_defenses:
      - NFKC normalization rescan (PI-010)
      - Hex/base64 decode and rescan (PI-006)
      - Case-insensitive matching
      - Whitespace-tolerant matching
    whitelist: project-scoped, time-bounded entries in .sdd/security/whitelist.sdd
    rules:
      - [PI-01] ALL user prompts scanned before dispatch
      - [PI-02] Internal agent-to-agent messages NOT scanned
      - [PI-03] BLOCK halts all processing immediately
      - [PI-04] All attempts audited via SHA-256 hash
      - [PI-12] Pattern registry loaded from .sdd/specs, not hard-coded

  ThreatModel:
  A threat model MUST document:
    Assets
    Trust boundaries
    Data flows
    Threat categories
    Mitigations
    Residual risk

  Threat model is updated when:
    architecture changes
    new external integration added
    new data sensitivity level introduced
    public exposure changes

State: +
  Note:
  This file is the threat model for the
  project. It uses STRIDE and OWASP Top 10 as threat categories.
  Concrete threat models are created per domain when real project
  analysis justifies them.
